        "raw": "<p>So, okay. My friends and I were playing this one the other day, and kind of got to wondering...&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">What&#39;s to stop the hero with the last turn from just standing in front of the train, preventing it from moving more than once space, and then next round getting up (if the attack incapacitated them) and repeating the effect? Meanwhile, the other heroes whale on the train, and yes, Ambuscade will probably get a lot of kills in in the meantime... but that won&#39;t actually get the train moving any faster. We were playing that way, and Ambuscade&#39;s player noted &quot;I don&#39;t think there&#39;s any way for me to win this. Although I&#39;m having fun killing you all repeatedly, definitely.&quot;<br /><br />I mean, I&#39;m trying to think of what Ambuscade could do. Rig the monorail line with explosives, and hope that&#39;s enough to kill the last person to go (who goes between ambuscade&#39;s last turn and the train moving) and that nobody else placed themselves as a backup train-blocker, or that he can kill them on his last turn of the round? I mean, it COULD work, but all you would really need is a fairly tough or mobile (or both) hero willing to take one for the team each round, and odds are good out of the rest, even if they&#39;re being incapactiated EVERY ROUND, will be able to do SOME damage to the monorail each round with even one power.</span></p>",
