      {
        "id": 118185,
        "name": "Benhimself",
        "username": "Benhimself",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/benhimself/{size}/2160_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-17T00:15:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ambuscade would need to push someone far enough that, even with a move AND a sprint, they couldn't get in front of the train. And that's a tall order when most heroes have 2^ movement, and no few can get mobility with at least one power! And like I said, if two heroes playing defense, ambuscade would have to incap-overkill them BOTH to that extent.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I suspect \"get all players to really low health, and rig the rail with explosives\" MIGHT work, because then they're incapped on their turn. But it is only a 4 die attack. And if someone is knocked out by the train itself Ambuscade will have to kill them ENTIRELY with explosives, since they get up at the start of their turn with full health. It's a strategy I'm interested in trying but I'm wondering if A) anyone has tried it and it worked out for them or not, or B) If anyone has won as Ambuscade in any other way.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:51:03.237Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
